{"content":[{"id":"5d9c2f4a","settings":{"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[{"id":"4ee32429","settings":{"editor":"<p>When your air conditioner hums, struggles to start, or stops cooling, a failing capacitor may be the reason. This component helps the compressor and fan motors start. When it weakens, your AC may short cycle, trip the breaker, or run without the outdoor fan spinning.<\/p><p>Most AC capacitor problems are repairable when caught early. This guide explains the warning signs, causes, costs, and what homeowners should do next.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1feaf046","settings":{"title":"Quick Answer: What Should You Know About AC Capacitor Problems?","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2.5,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"51b164aa","settings":{"editor":"<p>Common signs include humming from the outdoor unit, slow startup, a condenser fan that will not spin, repeated breaker trips, and an AC that turns on and off too often.<\/p><p>Professional replacement often falls between $100 and $400 nationally. The actual price depends on the part, labor, timing, and related damage. Because capacitors can retain a dangerous charge after power is turned off, replacement is not a safe DIY project.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"620c62c2","settings":{"title":"What Does an AC Capacitor Do?","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2.5,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2532e13d","settings":{"editor":"<p>An AC capacitor <a href=\"https:\/\/www.lennox.com\/residential\/lennox-life\/consumer\/what%27s-an-ac-capacitor\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">stores and releases electrical energy<\/a>. It gives the compressor and fan motors the boost they need to start and helps them continue operating.<\/p><p>Many central air conditioners use a dual run capacitor for the compressor and outdoor fan. If one side fails, the indoor blower may still move air while the outdoor unit does not work correctly.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"17b881e5","settings":{"title":"Warning Signs of a Failing AC Capacitor","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2.5,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"46b4cc3b","settings":{"title":"The Outdoor Unit Hums but Does Not Start","header_size":"p","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"9cb5ad","settings":{"editor":"<p>Humming often means a motor is receiving power but cannot get the boost needed to start. Turn the system off instead of letting it keep trying. Repeated failed starts can damage a motor.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3863bc4f","settings":{"title":"The Condenser Fan Is Not Spinning","header_size":"p","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3dac201a","settings":{"editor":"<p>If the indoor system is running but the outdoor fan is still, the capacitor may be weak or failed. A bad fan motor, damaged wiring, or control problem can cause the same symptom, so testing matters.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"772ea668","settings":{"title":"The AC Starts Slowly or Short Cycles","header_size":"p","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"62c8cb3e","settings":{"editor":"<p>A weak capacitor can delay startup or cause the system to turn on and off too frequently. Airflow restrictions, thermostat problems, and refrigerant issues can create similar symptoms.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"47d7942e","settings":{"title":"The Breaker Keeps Tripping","header_size":"p","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2f37a07","settings":{"editor":"<p>A motor that cannot start properly may draw too much current. If the breaker trips more than once, leave it off and schedule service. Repeated resets can cause more damage.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"ecf233a","settings":{"title":"What Causes AC Capacitors to Fail?","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2.5,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3a946026","settings":{"editor":"<p>Capacitors wear down over time, but prolonged heat and heavy system use can speed up the process. During hot, humid July weather in New Rochelle and lower Westchester, an already weakened capacitor may fail when the AC is working hardest.<\/p><p>Other causes include:<\/p><ul><li>Heat buildup inside the outdoor unit<\/li><li>Normal age and electrical wear<\/li><li>Power surges or voltage fluctuations<\/li><li>Loose or overheated connections<\/li><li>A motor or compressor drawing excessive current<\/li><li>An incorrectly rated replacement part<\/li><\/ul><p>Sometimes the capacitor is the only failed component. In other cases, another problem is placing too much strain on it. Preparing the system before peak cooling season may help technicians identify developing electrical issues. Review these <a href=\"https:\/\/gcreliable.com\/blog\/spring-hvac-maintenance-tips\">spring HVAC maintenance tips<\/a> for additional ways to prepare your equipment for warmer weather.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"72221bff","settings":{"title":"What Should You Do Right Now?","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2.5,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"219fa130","settings":{"editor":"<p>If the outdoor unit is humming, the fan is not spinning, or the breaker keeps tripping, turn the AC off at the thermostat.<\/p><p>You can safely check the thermostat setting, air filter, and breaker once. Do not keep resetting the breaker, remove the electrical panel, or touch the capacitor and wiring.<\/p><p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.gcreliable.com\/systems\/air-conditioning\/ac-repair\">Schedule an inspection<\/a> if the system still will not start or cool. Acting early may help prevent compressor or fan motor damage.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3d33180","settings":{"title":"How Is a Bad AC Capacitor Diagnosed?","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2.5,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"73740a32","settings":{"editor":"<p>A <a href=\"https:\/\/gcreliable.com\/about-us\">qualified HVAC technician<\/a> should confirm the failure rather than replace a part based on symptoms alone.<\/p><p>The process may include:<\/p><ul><li>Inspecting the capacitor for swelling, leaking, corrosion, or burned connections<\/li><li>Measuring its capacitance and comparing the reading with the rated tolerance<\/li><li>Checking the contactor, wiring, compressor, and fan motor<\/li><li>Testing system startup after the repair<\/li><\/ul><p>This helps determine whether the capacitor caused the breakdown or failed because of another problem.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"48032462","settings":{"title":"How Much Does AC Capacitor Replacement Cost?","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2.5,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3435e9f3","settings":{"editor":"<p>Professional replacement <a href=\"https:\/\/www.carrier.com\/us\/en\/residential\/hvac-resources\/air-conditioners\/ac-capacitor\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">commonly costs about $100 to $400<\/a> as a national estimate. Local pricing varies based on the capacitor type, labor, emergency scheduling, equipment access, and related damage.<\/p><p>Before approving the repair, ask whether the quote includes diagnosis, installation, testing, and any warranty. A clear estimate should also explain whether the capacitor is the only issue.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4057b186","settings":{"title":"Is Replacing a Bad Capacitor Worth It?","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2.5,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1ab97bda","settings":{"editor":"<p>In most cases, yes. A capacitor is a relatively minor repair and is not, by itself, a reason to replace the entire air conditioner.<\/p><p>Repair usually makes sense when the rest of the system is in good condition. If testing reveals a failing compressor, damaged motor, repeated electrical problems, or an older system with several recent repairs, ask for both repair and replacement options.<\/p><p>Consider the total cost, system age, repair history, efficiency, and expected reliability before deciding.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"134b15cc","settings":{"title":"Frequently Asked Questions About AC Capacitor Problems","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2.5,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"341d80f1","settings":{"items":[{"item_title":"How long does an AC capacitor last?","_id":"8728ce6"},{"item_title":"Can a weak capacitor increase my electric bill?","_id":"a06a071"},{"item_title":"Can an AC tune-up find a weak capacitor?","_id":"5da94bc"},{"item_title":"Will replacing the capacitor always fix weak cooling?","_id":"3980c5c"}],"faq_schema":"yes","title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[{"id":"9b4f93b","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[{"id":"27f57b58","settings":{"editor":"<p>Many capacitors last several years, and some remain in service for a decade or longer. Heavy use, heat exposure, voltage problems, and part quality can shorten their lifespan.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"16cf5ded","settings":{"_title":"item #2","content_width":"full","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[{"id":"2bd49da7","settings":{"editor":"<p>It can. A struggling motor may take longer to start or operate less efficiently. Other AC problems can <a href=\"https:\/\/gcreliable.com\/blog\/4-tips-for-cutting-cooling-costs-in-scarsdale-ny\">also raise energy use<\/a>, so testing is needed.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"7746ac0e","settings":{"_title":"item #3","content_width":"full","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[{"id":"5f6b494a","settings":{"editor":"<p>Yes. <a href=\"https:\/\/gcreliable.com\/systems\/maintenance\">During maintenance<\/a>, a technician can <a href=\"https:\/\/www.energystar.gov\/saveathome\/heating-cooling\/maintenance-checklist\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">test the capacitor<\/a> and determine whether its output remains within the manufacturer\u2019s acceptable range.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"756c37f7","settings":{"_title":"item #3","content_width":"full","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[{"id":"3afd76ec","settings":{"editor":"<p>No. Weak cooling can also result from low refrigerant, dirty coils, airflow restrictions, a failing compressor, or duct problems. The capacitor should be tested before replacement.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true}],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"nested-accordion","elType":"widget"},{"id":"59bb3b22","settings":{"title":"Get a Clear Diagnosis Before a Small Problem Causes More Damage","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"brandon-grotesque","typography_font_size":{"unit":"rem","size":2.5,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"rem","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile_extra":{"unit":"rem","size":1.7,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1,"sizes":[]},"ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"47313309","settings":{"editor":"<p>AC capacitor problems are often manageable when addressed early. If your outdoor unit is humming, the fan will not start, or the breaker keeps tripping, stop running the system and have it inspected.<\/p><p>G.C. Reliable Service has served New Rochelle and Westchester County since 1980. <a href=\"https:\/\/gcreliable.com\/contact-us\">Contact the team<\/a> for professional AC repair, clear recommendations, and an upfront explanation of your options before work begins.<\/p>","ha_cmc_text":"Happy Addons"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"}],"settings":{"template":"default"},"metadata":[]}